{title: More Love to Thee}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: author Elizabeth Prentiss}
{meta: author William Doane}
{meta: year 1869}
{meta: died 1878}
{meta: died 1915}
{meta: source WorshipCommons, https://worshipcommons.org/songs/znPVOl0yZza}
{copyright: Public domain}

Verse 1
[Eb]More love to [Bb]thee, O [Eb]Christ, more [Ab]love to [Bb]thee!
[Eb]Hear thou the [Bb]prayer I [Cm]make on [Ab]bended [Bb]knee;
[Eb]this is my [Bb]earnest [Eb]plea: more [Ab]love, O [Eb]Christ, to [Bb]thee,
[Eb]more love to [Ab]thee, [Eb]more [Bb]love to [Eb]thee!

Verse 2
Once earthly joy I craved, sought peace and rest;
Now Thee alone I seek, give what is best;
This all my pray'r shall be: more love, O Christ, to Thee,
More love to Thee, more love to Thee!

Verse 3
Then shall my latest breath whisper Thy praise;
This be the parting cry my heart shall raise;
This still its pray'r shall be: more love, O Christ, to Thee,
More love to Thee, more love to Thee!
